---

## SCHEMA VALIDATION

### Validation Rules

Every schema MUST:

1. Be valid JSON
2. Validate against JSON Schema Draft 2020-12
3. Use `$schema` field pointing to 2020-12
4. Use `$id` field with unique URI
5. Have `title` and `description`
6. Define all `required` fields
7. Use `additionalProperties: false` for strict validation
8. Document every field with `description`
9. Include `enum` where values are fixed
10. Include `pattern` where format is defined
11. Include `format` where applicable
12. Be consistent with related schemas

### Validation Checklist

- [ ] Schema is valid JSON
- [ ] Schema is valid JSON Schema 2020-12
- [ ] All properties documented
- [ ] All required fields defined
- [ ] No circular references
- [ ] References resolve correctly
- [ ] Types are consistent
- [ ] Enums are exhaustive
- [ ] Patterns are correct
- [ ] Examples validate against schema

---

## SUCCESS CRITERIA

Schema Engine phase is successful when:

1. All required schemas generated
2. All schemas valid JSON Schema
3. All schemas documented
4. All schemas internally consistent
5. All schemas validated against examples
6. All references resolve
7. No circular dependencies
8. Passes schema validation

